            <ArticleTitle>[A 40-year old male presented with a painful cord running over his chest].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>A3222</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This disease, Mondor's disease, is a self-limiting disease caused by a thrombophlebitis of the superficial epigastric and thoracic veins. In this case repetitive injury sustained from running was probably the cause.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
